Root cause:
The MAC comparison in tcp_ao_verify_hash used `memcmp`, which is not constant-time, allowing timing side-channel attacks that could leak MAC values.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (memcmp(phash, hash_buf, maclen)) {
```
Reason:
`memcmp` is not constant-time, meaning its execution time may depend on the first differing byte. An attacker who can measure timing can thus deduce the MAC value, enabling side-channel attacks.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#include <crypto/utils.h>
```
```c
